WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.220
Everyone, this Friendship Cup.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.950
Do you know what happens to 
the losers of these duels?

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.420
They're sent to an underground 
waste-processing facility!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.430
I tried to tell the people the truth about 
the Friendship Cup, but no one cared.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.030
I will be the one...

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.130
...to win!

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.690
No... This isn't right.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.210
This isn't the type of duel I believe in!

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.690
Don't do this!

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.920
Don't take him underground!

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:41.910
Get away.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.590
Let me go!

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.010
Please, let me go!

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.580
D-Wheels.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.840
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.480
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.940
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.130
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.570
Dragon Slaying!! 
Hugo Versus Sawatari

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.300
Why did I fight the duel that way?

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:55.520
Because of me... that man 
was sent underground.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.390
The next match of the Friendship Cup

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.310
will be Hugo versus Shingo Sawatari!

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:03.960
Sawatari?

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.160
Him, eh?

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.850
Not again! Why Shingo?

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.230
When will Shingo Sawatari get his turn?!

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.730
Shingo...

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.640
That's me!

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.230
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.750
It's finally here... The moment 
I've been waiting for.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.700
Watch me, Rin.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.460
I'm going to keep my promise to you and win.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:40.900
That's right. Maybe I should tell them about 
the dimensional war, in Yuzu's place.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.370
Sorry for the wait, everyone.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.610
The duelists will now enter the arena!

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:48.810
Hey!

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.780
First up, Hugo!

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.920
Next, Shingo Sawatari!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.120
Sorry for the wait!

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:04.360
The Friendship Cup's leading man, 
Shingo Sawatari, has arrived!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.220
Who the hell are you?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.480
Leading man, my foot!

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.580
No one knows who you are!

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.640
Yeah! Do something!

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.770
Hugo...

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.520
A fired-up crowd. An audience waiting to cheer.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.130
Truly, this stage is made for me!

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.150
You'd better fight a good duel, okay?

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:33.320
Right back at you, man.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.160
I hope you duel as well as you talk.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.680
The sparks are already flying 
on the starting line.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.890
Now, let's get going!

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.530
Action Field, on.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:48.370
Field Spell Crossover Acceleration!

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.710
Duel Mode, on. Autopilot, stand by.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.250
Riding duel...

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.620
Acceleration!

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.220
Duel!

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.460
I'm taking the first move!

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.670
He passed him!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.870
Shingo Sawatari is first around the 
corner, taking the first move!

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.880
That was close...

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.370
Not bad at all.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.840
You see my fantastic riding technique, do you?

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.360
But now, for the main event.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.450
The curtain rises on the entertainment theater!

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.190
I'm about to show you the ultimate performance.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.190
My turn!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:46.860
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 3 Abyss Actor — Extras

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:52.300
and Scale 8 Abyss Actor — Funky Comedian!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:02.010
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and 7 simultaneously.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.940
Pendulum Summon!

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:07.500
Come out, my servants!

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.200
First, Abyss Actor — Superstar!

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:16.990
Then, Abyss Actor — Sassy Rookie!

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:23.020
Shingo Sawatari's entertainment theater 
kicks off with a Pendulum Summon!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.230
I see you're not all talk, huh?

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.430
There's more excitement to come...

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:33.000
Superstar's effect lets me add an Abyss 
Script from my deck to my hand.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:34.570
I activate it!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.710
Abyss Script — Opening Ceremony!

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.680
Its effect lets me gain 500 life points

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:51.130
for every Abyss Actor on my side 
of the field in attack position.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.690
I have two monsters. Thus, I gain 1000 life points!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.030
And I end my turn.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.460
Now, it's your turn.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.810
Don't mind if I do!

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.040
My turn!

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:19.420
If I have no other monsters on my side of the 
field, I can Special Summon this card.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.970
Come out, Speedroid Terrortop!

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.860
When there's a Wind Attribute 
Monster on my field,

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:31.080
I can Special Summon this 
monster from my hand.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.150
Come out, Speedroid Taketomborg!

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:41.570
And I Normal Summon Tuner Monster 
Red-Eyed Dice, from my hand!

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:51.820
Level 1 Red-Eyed Dice

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:55.140
tunes Level 3 Terrortop and Taketomborg!

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.000
Flap your beautiful and heroic wings,

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.180
to strike the enemy at the speed of light.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:09.770
Synchro Summon!

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:15.430
Appear, Level 7 Clear Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:20.430
Hugo performs the Synchro 
Summon without a hitch!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.820
Level 7 and 2500 attack points... 
What a powerful monster!

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.130
Hugo...

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:33.760
A dragon, huh? A perfect villain for my show.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.890
Sawatari's entertainment theater 
will feature a dragon-slaying.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:41.500
I'll cut it down with one stroke!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.130
Try it, if you can.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.740
I attack Sassy Rookie with 
Clear Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.740
I activate Sassy Rookie's monster effect!

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:56.780
Once per turn, I negate its destruction.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.150
But you still take damage!

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.320
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.070
The life Shingo Sawatari went to such trouble 
to obtain was shaved away in a second!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.260
Will he lose his spot in the leading role?

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.990
Odd-Eyes...

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.910
My turn! Draw!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.180
That damage was nothing.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:31.150
As long as I have Pendulum Summon,

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:36.120
the leading entertainment theater 
actor will be I, Shingo Sawatari.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:41.980
I activate my Continuous Trap Dragon's 
Bind, targeting Clear Wing!

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.240
This lets me negate the Special 
Summon of a monster

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.200
with fewer attack points than Clear Wing has.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:54.800
Now, you can only Pendulum Summon 
monsters with 2500 or more attack points.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.800
Cutting off my Pendulum?

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:02.250
And I activate my Continuous Trap Follow 
Wing, with Clear Wing as its target!

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.560
Now, Clear Wing can't be destroyed by battle.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:12.270
And any monster that it fights, 
Level 5 or below, is destroyed,

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:15.290
which adds its attack points to Clear Wing's!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.220
It can't be destroyed, and it 
also destroys my monsters

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:21.030
to increase its own attack points?

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.400
Now, everything's in place.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.270
You're the one about to be slain!

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.580
Not bad at all...

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:33.440
But a show isn't exciting if the villain isn't strong.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.820
I summon Abyss Actor — Leading 
Lady from my hand!

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:48.120
Forced to Normal Summon a Level 4 monster?

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.300
But that monster can't beat Clear Wing.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.240
You think not?

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:57.870
There are ways to get rid of 
Clear Wing besides battle.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:01.930
If I use Superstar's effect to acquire 
Abyss Script — Fantasy Magic,

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:06.070
its effect will let me return one 
of your monsters to your hand.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.300
I'm the leading man in this entertainment duel!

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.450
I activate Superstar's effect!

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:17.140
In that instant, I activate Clear 
Wing's monster effect!

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:21.190
When a monster on the field, Level 5 
or above, activates its effect,

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:25.030
I can negate that effect and destroy the monster!

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.750
Dichroic Mirror!

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.560
Damn...

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:39.400
Clear Wing also seals the effects 
of monsters, Level 5 or above.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:43.450
Clear Wing has higher billing.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.950
But...

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:50.480
If I win, Sawatari will be sent underground.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.020
Huh? If I?

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:56.830
I activate Continuous Spell

00:11:56.830 --> 00:12:00.170
Abyss Prop — Wild Wagon from my hand!

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:05.440
You think I'll sit by and let you beat me?

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:08.030
Retreat is the last of the thirty-six great strategies!

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:13.240
Leading Lady and Rookie ran away!

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.270
You won't escape!

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:35.300
Will the dragon catch the retreating Sassy Rookie 
and Leading Lady in its evil clutches?

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.970
What will their fate be?

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.310
You can't run away! Give up already!

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:46.910
Don't be ridiculous, wicked user of dragons...

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.560
You servant of evil!

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.800
I end my turn!

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:54.350
Dichroic Mirror's effect ends 
during your End Phase.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.170
Its attack points return to normal.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.630
My turn!

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:03.830
I attack Leading Lady with Clear 
Wing Synchro Dragon!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.670
With this...

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:09.900
...I'll deal 1000 points of damage.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:15.610
The cowardly, evil dragon skips the 
knight, going straight for the lady!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:18.840
I activate Abyss Prop — Wild Wagon's effect!

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:24.350
Once per turn, I can negate the destruction 
of one Abyss Actor Pendulum Monster.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.820
But you still take the damage!

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:38.300
Taking damage lets me activate 
Leading Lady's monster effect!

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:43.260
Once per turn, I can lower one 
monster's original attack points

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.870
by the amount of damage I took!

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:52.840
In other words, Clear Wing's attack 
points go from 2500 to 1500!

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:58.220
You really thought I had no countermeasures?

00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:59.020
Take this!

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.890
Clear Wing's effect activates!

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:08.830
When it's targeted by the effect of 
a monster, Level 5 or above...

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.800
...the effect is negated, and the monster is destroyed!

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.270
Dichroic Mirror!

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.100
Wild Wagon's second effect!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.570
Leading Lady, as a target of this card,

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:27.850
is unaffected by your spell, trap, 
and monster effects this turn!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:36.790
Reducing Clear Wing's attack points 
dilutes the effect of Dragon's Bind.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:40.270
In other words, I can Pendulum 
Summon as many monsters,

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.260
with 1500 attack points or more, as I want!

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:45.960
Looks like you're the one who's 
up against the wall now.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.930
What a turnaround!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.600
We thought Shingo Sawatari was cornered,

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:53.870
but it's Hugo who's trapped now!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.440
Hugo...

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.550
You're not bad at all.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:02.180
But I won't lose that easily!

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:03.920
I end my turn!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:07.840
Starting to realize how awesome 
I am? But it's a bit too late.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.120
I'm going to lower the curtain on 
the Sawatari Theater's final act!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.820
My turn!

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:17.360
With the Pendulum Scale already 
set, I Pendulum Summon!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.420
Return from my Extra Deck, Superstar!

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:26.300
Superstar is back on the field!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:30.740
And I activate Funky Comedian's Pendulum Effect!

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:34.210
I send Superstar to my Extra Deck,

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:40.420
to add its attack points to Sassy 
Rookie's until my End Phase.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:44.620
I attack Clear Wing with Sassy Rookie!

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:49.690
Sassy Rookie is Level 4, and it's thus 
unaffected by Follow Wing.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:55.600
Hugo takes 2700 damage, all at once!

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.910
Now, I use Leading Lady's monster effect

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:03.270
to reduce Clear Wing's attack points 
by the battle damage I took!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:08.980
Incredible! Clear Wing Synchro Dragon's 
attack points are down to 0!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.600
It's over...

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:12.810
You have 1300 life left.

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:15.850
Leading Lady will end this with her final kiss.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:19.090
Is Hugo's time on the stage at an end?!

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:21.790
Now, time for the climax!

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:25.830
I attack Clear Wing with Leading Lady!

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.530
An Action Card!

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.600
Hugo got an Action Card!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.390
I activate Action Spell Miracle!

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:42.560
I negate the destruction of one monster by battle,

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.450
and halve the damage dealt!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.360
He held out!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.590
Y-Yuya?

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:58.490
So the curtain hasn't lowered yet, eh?

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:01.800
I haven't had a duel this exciting in a while!

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:06.620
But as I keep saying, I'm the leading 
man of entertainment duels.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.800
I'll finish this on my next turn.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.130
For now, I end my turn!

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:17.560
Hugo just barely holds out, 
but his life is a mere 550!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.720
Can he find a way to fight back?!

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:20.520
Yes!

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:22.520
As long as I get that card!

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:24.260
My turn!

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.790
Draw!

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.080
Draw!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.000
I got it!

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:40.200
I summon Speedroid Double 
Yoyo from my hand!

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.720
When I summon this card,

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:48.710
I can Special Summon one Speedroid monster, 
Level 3 or below, from my graveyard!

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:52.230
I Special Summon Red-Eyed Dice!

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.190
A Synchro Summon, eh?

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:03.790
A bit late for another side character's debut.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:09.220
Level 1 Red-Eyed Dice tunes 
Level 4 Double Yoyo!

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:18.960
Shining body embraced by twin wings...

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:22.250
Use those wings to fly to the heavens!

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:25.170
Synchro Summon!

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:30.280
Come out, Level 5 Hi-Speedroid Hagoita!

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:35.370
I tribute Hagoita

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:39.500
to grant its effect to all monsters on the field.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.330
Grant its effect?

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:48.010
Yeah. When any monster on 
the field changes its level,

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:50.870
that level is increased by one!

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.000
How pointless.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.210
You're already finished.

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:57.580
You're the one who's finished!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.020
The fun is only getting started!

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:08.250
I activate my spell card Hi-Speed Re-Level!

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:12.830
By banishing one Speedroid in my graveyard,

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:17.800
I can set the levels of all monsters on the 
field to that of the banished Hagoita.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.500
All monsters are Level 5!

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:25.980
And Hagoita's effect means 
they all gain one more level!

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:32.970
This is why you took the trouble of tributing 
Hagoita and conferring its effect?

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:36.790
I activate Clear Wing's monster effect!

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:40.680
Now that Leading Lady and Sassy 
Rookie are over Level 5,

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:43.050
I negate their effects and destroy them!

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.180
Dichroic Mirror!

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:54.080
The attack points of Leading 
Lady and Sassy Rookie

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.040
are 1500 and 1700.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.940
Thus, Clear Wing's attack points become 3200!

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:06.250
Go, Clear Wing Synchro Dragon.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:10.250
Attack Shingo Sawatari directly!

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:22.200
Whirlwind Hell Dive Slasher!

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:30.010
It's over!

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:33.360
Turnaround after turnaround... 
What an incredible duel!

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:37.180
And the one who seized victory 
at the end was Hugo!

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:50.330
Yeah... I got through the first round.

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:53.160
Though I think I got a little overexcited.

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:58.700
Huh? I feel like there's something 
I'm supposed to say.

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:01.170
Oh, well...

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.500
Hugo became Yuya...

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:07.930
Damn! I almost had him!

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:11.350
You rock, Sawatari!

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:13.690
The Sawatari entertainment theater rocks!

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.120
Look over here!

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.680
You did great!

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:19.600
Mr. Sawatari!

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:25.640
Look! The crowd is on their feet for 
Sawatari Shingo's curtain call!

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:28.360
Hey!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.700
What are you doing? Respond to them!

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.200
Don't you hear their cheers?

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:37.240
They were impressed by our duel!

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:42.950
You know, you look a lot like Yuya.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.680
So I've heard.

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:48.970
No, I mean exactly like him.

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.370
You could be his twin brother.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:56.430
That's quite enough. Now, come along.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.050
S-Sawatari...

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:49.740
Welcome to hell on Earth.

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:52.190
Those who lose on the surface world,

00:23:52.190 --> 00:23:53.940
those who are given up on,

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:57.660
those abandoned as useless... 
They all fall down here.

00:23:58.100 --> 00:24:01.050
City is about competition, 
no matter where you go.

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:04.700
Those who lose will fall even lower!

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:08.590
For the sake of City... Dig, dig, and keep digging!

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:13.360
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Losers Who Crawl in the Dirt.

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:15.260
The fun is only getting started!
